   "id": 504707,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Determine if 1,429 is prime or composite.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>You only need to check numbers up to the square root of 1,429, which is approximately 37.80.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Use the known rules of divisibility.</p>\n<p>2: The last digit is even.</p>\n<p>The last digit is not even.</p>\n<p>3: Add the digits of the number together. If that sum is divisible by 3, then so is the original number.</p>\n<p>1 + 4 + 2 + 9 = 16</p>\n<p>16 is not divisible by 3.</p>\n<p>5: If the last digit is 5 or 0, then the original number is divisible by 5.</p>\n<p>The last digit is not 5 or 0, so the number is not divisible by 5.</p>\n<p>Step 2:</p>\n<p>Use a calculator to test the primes up to 37.</p>\n<p>7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23, 29, 31, 37</p>\n<p>For instance, 1,429 ÷ 7 ≈ 178.4285714.</p>\n<p>None of these primes result in an integer quotient. They all have a decimal part.</p>\n<p>The conclusion is that 1,429 is a prime number.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "Yes, 1,429 is prime."
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
